# This root file documents the configuration boundary.
# Runtime configuration lives in backend/.env and frontend/.env respectively.
# Copy each application's .env.example to .env; never put secrets in VITE_*.
# Database and AWS credentials are not needed for local report input or Phase 3 mock text generation.
# backend/.env AI_PROVIDER selects mock, bedrock, or disabled; see README for Bedrock setup.
# npm run setup:local prepares local PostgreSQL and fills missing backend/.env database/phone keys.
# Phase 4 uses private backend/data/reports files; Secrets Manager/SSM/S3 are not required.
# NAVER Maps uses frontend/.env VITE_NAVER_MAP_CLIENT_ID for map/address features.
